A||||5||KnightRyder31||Car problems||||1||
Z||000000||KnightRyder31||08-10-2000||06:35 PM||||It seems that I lost my pasing gear(well, it feels that way)...you know when your going like 20-25MPH and you floor it, how it kicks down a gear and pulls hard, I lost that!!! Also, when I come to a stop, my car viabrates like hell! WTF!?!?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Linx||08-10-2000||06:57 PM||||Wowsers!  I had the same problems two weeks ago!  My SE would idle real rough, and wouldnt upshift when accelerating.  It'd stick in 2nd.   Couldnt get it to downshift to accelerate either.  To my surprise...I found a spark plug had come loose.  Really loose.  Im not saying yours is loose...but that you might have an ignition problem.<P>Now- why the loose plug would affect the idle is obvious, but why it would keep my car from shifting is another thing altogether.  I thought it was two separate problems until i reseated the plug and my car became a rocket again.<p>[This message has been edited by Linx (edited 08-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierospeeder||08-10-2000||07:53 PM||||Theres a TV cable, i think thats what its called that goes from the linkage, to the transmission,  looks exactly like a throttle cable,  check to see if its not disconnected.<P>Does it only do it at 20mph.  But okay at the other speeds?<P>You can also drive in 2nd gear and push it in 1st and see if that works.||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||08-10-2000||08:46 PM||||Sounds like the Torque control converter. Thats what it does. Try this...get up to around 40 or 50 mph...while STILL pressing the accelerator, slightly press the brake w/ your left foot...the RPM should shoot up (car downshifts)..if it dosnt, its prob. your TCC...Ogre would be a better help than me, but that would definantly be my guess.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||KnightRyder31||08-10-2000||09:39 PM||||FieroSpeeder, wouldnt that hurt the transmission if I downshifted manualy??? I thought it might be the spark plug, I'll check it. Hey, how hard is it to change a alternater belt?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||08-11-2000||12:18 PM||||TC lock problems usually stall the car. A TC lock problem Could mess up kick down but it's more likely to make kickdown really harsh then anything. It should still kick down into second.<P>Down shift manually usually won't hurt an auto tranny. Most won't down shift if you are going to fast to do it safely. I'm not sure if this is true of the TH125. I've never messed with it like that.<P>Downshifting probly won't tell you what you want to know.<P>The hardest part is that you need to figure out if what is wrong is really a downshift or a TC lock problem. <P>Often what feels like a down shift in TH125 is really the TC unlocking. If there is a problem with the TC lock that is keeping the clutch from engaging then it can feel like you've lost a gear.<P>The easy test for TC lock is to press the brake while doing a constant speed over <B>35mph.</B> (The test WILL NOT work if you are accelerating or slowing.) You only need press the pedal enough to activate a switch. (about 1") If the TC is workig right you should see the tach jump up about 200RPM then drop again when you let off the brake.<P>the second TC test is to pull the TC lock's electrical connector. It's on the front of the tranny. unplug it and see if you still have problems.<P>If the TC tests pass then you have either a TV cable problem or the tranny has internal problems. In this case you say it happens at 20-25mph. So that makes it look like TV or internal problems. Do the TC tests anyway just to make sure.<P>((I think I just found my next cave article. I wonder how many times I've typed something like this    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ))<P>------------------<BR>Lake Superior? Is that what I stepped in? Sorry.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-11-2000).]||||reg||1
